<properties>
{"title":"Brady's Story"}
</properties>
<content>
<callout icon="\">
	Know this story. On a closer call, you're not just selling a program — you're selling Brady. When a prospect hesitates, this story is what closes them.
</callout>
### Who Is Brady?
Brady is a 22-year-old from the Chicago suburbs who went to Iowa. In high school he was a dead-broke Walmart stoner; in college he was the broke frat kid. Instead of waiting for a degree to pay off, he built **onebuzz**, a college media company that did roughly **\$1M in revenue** and grew to about **1M followers**. Then he built [**Seatstock.com**](http://Seatstock.com) — a ticketing platform that reached about a **quarter-million users**, approached **8-figure revenue**, employed a **40-person team**, and raised **\$600–700K — at 19 years old**.
When he found UGC, he made **\$10K in his first month**. He realized the space was full of creators who could make content but had no idea how to run it like a business — so he started **The Vault** to teach creators how to land and scale brand deals through Sideshift, backed by real agency-side brand relationships.
Positioning in one line: **"a decently cool kid in a really dorky space."** He's relatable and normal, but connected — Sideshift leadership, Whop co-founders. He is not a UGC robot, and neither are we on calls.
### His UGC Philosophy
- **"UGC is like a business — good services get paid higher premiums."** Most creators price themselves like commodities and stack cheap deals. The Vault teaches them to price up and treat content like a service business.
- **The creator economy is rich-get-richer.** Good content compounds — the same video keeps paying month after month. The poor get poorer by grinding low CPM deals.
- The space is **early** — roughly 1M creators on Sideshift. Brands are moving newbies to CPM-only deals while big brands pay retainers with view minimums. The window to build positioning is now.
- Myths he attacks on calls: "deals are concrete," "you need experience first," "take every deal you can get," "UGC is for randoms, not real influencers."
### His Results
- **\~\$15K MRR** (June 2026) — all organic, zero paid ads
- **\$200K+ in creator payouts** generated for members
- Average member: **\~\$6.5K/month after about 45 days**
- Goal: \$100K months and the biggest info product in the UGC space
### Why The Vault Exists
Brady's 5-year vision: change 1,000s of lives with UGC and sit on the cap table of a massive company. The UGC education space is full of placement mills running creators like slave labor on cheap CPM deals. The Vault is the opposite: real education (content, business, negotiation), real feedback from top-100 creators, and real brand relationships that place members on deals.
### Key Talking Points — Use These On Calls
- Built two real companies before 22: onebuzz (\~\$1M revenue, \~1M followers) and Seatstock (\~250K users, 40 staff, raised \$600–700K at 19). He's done this outside of UGC too.
- Made \$10K his own first month in UGC — the system is what he actually did.
- Members average \~\$6.5K/month after \~45 days; \$200K+ paid out to creators so far.
- Connected where it matters: Sideshift leadership and Whop co-founders. Deals come through real relationships, not cold pitching.
- Values that come through on calls: effort, winning, freedom, grit, "never be normal," show up every day.
### Catchphrases (use his language)
- "UGC is like a business — good services get paid higher premiums."
- "The UGC space has a creator economy right now — the rich get rich, the poor get poorer."
- "Aim for the moon, land in the stars at worst."
<callout icon="\">
	**COMPLIANCE — NON-NEGOTIABLE:** Never say "guaranteed brand deals." Brand deal placement is actively supported by the team — it is NOT guaranteed. The guarantee is: members make \$5K/month at some point (no time bound). Get this wrong and it's a legal liability for Brady.
</callout>
